# The fusions that owe no equality because nobody looked for double counting. One row per
# composed layer whose elimination search is `unmeasured`.
#
# Suspended is a third outcome
#   Beside passed and failed. A composer who states they never searched has not claimed their
#   figure equals the sum of its parts. Asserting the equality anyway is a checker inventing a claim
#   the document declined to make, which is the exact defect the search element was added to
#   prevent, arriving in the checker instead of in the document.
#
# A null `quantity` means every quantity
#   Its `quantity` is NULL, and that means every quantity rather than none. A composer who never
#   searched owes no sum for demand, nameplate or draw, so this arm is coarser than its sibling
#   eliminations/unsized.sqlc, which suspends exactly the quantity it was filed against. The union
#   carries the column so a caller can tell the two apart; read it as
#   `quantity IS NULL OR quantity = <the quantity being computed>`.
#
# `none` and `notApplicable` suspend nothing
#   "Somebody looked and found none" and "the question does not arise" both leave the sum rule
#   exact. Only "nobody looked" removes it.
-- eliminations/searched.sqlc, kept where asrt:absent/pm:reason is "unmeasured".
SELECT es.composition, es.composed_layer,
       NULL::pm.summed_quantity AS quantity,
       'the search was never made' AS suspended_because,
       es.note
FROM (
    :compose(eliminations/searched.sqlc)
) es
WHERE es.answer = 'unmeasured'
